On Fri, Nov 21, 2014 at 4:19 PM, la durka <durka42@gmail.com> wrote:

> Are we so sure {stanruasabi} isn't a type-3 fu'ivla? The fu'ivla types are
> just a convention anyway. I know the Book says the "tail" of a type-3
> fu'ivla should start with a consonant, but a glide {ua} is _nearly_ a
> consonant. Furthermore, syllable analysis (using camxes) gives us
> {sta,nr,ua,sa,bi} which has that telltale consonantal syllable.
>
> So I say {stanruasabi} is type-3 and fine. What do you think?
>

As you say, it's just a conventional name, nothing really hinges on that. I
agree it makes sense to include such things among type-3. But personally
I'd go with a full type-4, maybe "uaxsabi".

mu'o mi'e xorxes

